<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jacques Duchesne</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1837">1837</a>–<a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jacques Duchesne was a French general who commanded the expedition that conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a> in 1895. Marching inland from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahajanga">Mahajanga</a> with about 15,000 men, many of whom died of disease, he sent a flying column that reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antananarivo">Antananarivo</a> and shelled it into surrender on 30 September 1895. He had earlier served in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a> and in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sino-french-war">Sino-French War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jacques-duchesne.jpg" alt="Jacques Duchesne" width="320" height="589" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Félix Potin et Cie (vers 1900) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CFP_G%C3%A9n%C3%A9ral_Duchesne.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
